    <ferc:AttestationName id="f-321" contextRef="c-03">T.J. Winczewski</ferc:AttestationName>
    <ferc:AttestationTitle id="f-322" contextRef="c-03">Vice President</ferc:AttestationTitle>
    <ferc:NotesToFinancialStatementsTextBlock id="f-324" contextRef="c-03">&lt;div&gt;&lt;div class="Section_1"&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; font-size: 10pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Aptos; font-weight: bold; background-color: unset; font-size: 1em; text-align: inherit"&gt;The Company&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class="Section_1"&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 8pt; line-height: 116%"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Aptos"&gt;Wilprise Pipeline Company, L.L.C. (&amp;quot;Wilprise&amp;quot;), a Delaware limited liability company, is a wholly owned subsidiary of Enterprise Products Operating LLC, a Texas limited liability company (&amp;quot;EPOLLC&amp;quot;). EPOLLC in turn is wholly owned by Enterprise Products Partners L.P., a Delaware limited partnership, which is a publicly traded partnership. EPOLLC is the operator of Wilprise.&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 8pt; line-height: 116%"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Aptos; font-weight: bold"&gt;Description of the Property&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 8pt; line-height: 116%"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Aptos"&gt;Wilprise owns a 30-mile-long, 12&amp;quot; natural gas liquids (&amp;quot;NGL&amp;quot;) pipeline located entirely within the State of Louisiana. The pipeline receives NGLs from Tri-States NGL Pipeline, L.L.C. and delivers NGLs to Baton Rouge Pipeline LLC at the Sorrento Dome in Ascension Parish, Louisiana.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 8pt; line-height: 116%"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Aptos"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 8pt; line-height: 116%"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Aptos; font-weight: bold"&gt;Basis of Accounting&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 8pt; line-height: 116%"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Aptos"&gt;The accounting policies followed in preparation of these financial statements conform to those required by FERC. Financial statements are prepared on the accrual basis of accounting. Wilprise's property, plant and equipment assets are recorded at original cost.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 8pt; line-height: 116%"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Aptos"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 8pt; line-height: 116%"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Aptos; font-weight: bold"&gt;Revenue Recognition&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 8pt; line-height: 116%"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Aptos"&gt;Wilprise's revenues are derived from transportation of NGLs under a tariff regulated by the FERC. The tariff specifies the amounts to be paid by shippers for service between receipt and delivery locations and the general terms and conditions of transportation services on the pipeline system. Revenues are recorded upon receipt of products from customers.&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 8pt; line-height: 116%"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Aptos"&gt;During 2025, Wilprise Pipeline rebilled shippers for under-recovery resulting from the vacated January 20, 2022 rehearing order (Docket No. RM20-14-001) in the amount of $295,002. (See Commission's order issued on November 20, 2025 (Docket No. RM93-11-003, paragraph 37, footnote 111)). These revenues are reported in account 645 &amp;quot;Unusual or Infrequent Items (credit)&amp;quot; on page 114.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 8pt; line-height: 116%"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Aptos"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 8pt; line-height: 116%"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Aptos; font-weight: bold"&gt;Income Taxes&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 8pt; line-height: 116%"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Aptos"&gt;Wilprise is a limited liability company that passes income tax liability through the company to EPOLLC and does not recognize this liability on the company's financial statements. For purposes of calculating the income tax expense and liability for the annual cost of service (shown on page 700 of the Annual Report) Wilprise employs FERC's Policy Statement on Income Tax Allowances.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 8pt; line-height: 116%"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Aptos"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 8pt; line-height: 116%"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Aptos; font-weight: bold"&gt;Employees&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 8pt; line-height: 116%"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Aptos"&gt;Wilprise has no employees of its own. All operations, management, and administrative functions are performed by employees of Enterprise Products Company, on behalf of EPOLLC as operator.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Aptos"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Aptos"&gt;Wilprise reimburses EPOLLC for management and administrative functions under the terms of an operating agreement.&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 8pt; line-height: 116%"&gt; 				&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br style="page-break-before: always; clear: both" /&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 		&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:NotesToFinancialStatementsTextBlock>
    <ferc:StatementAboutImportantChangesDuringTheQuarterYearTextBlock id="f-326" contextRef="c-03">&lt;div class="Section_1"&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; font-size: 10pt"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;1) None&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; font-size: 10pt"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;2) None&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; font-size: 10pt"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;3) None&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; font-size: 10pt"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;4) None&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; font-size: 10pt"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;5) N/A&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 		&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:StatementAboutImportantChangesDuringTheQuarterYearTextBlock>
    <ferc:ReportDate id="f-328" contextRef="c-03">2026-04-16</ferc:ReportDate>
